v. (%)&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.calendar&quot;:&quot;Calendar Year&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.calendar-chart.hatching-legend&quot;:&quot;During this period performance was achieved under circumstances that no longer apply&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.calendar.fiveYear&quot;:&quot;5y&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.calendar.fourYear&quot;:&quot;4y&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.calendar.missingData&quot;:&quot;Missing calendar year returns data&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.calendar.oneYear&quot;:&quot;1y&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.calendar.threeYear&quot;:&quot;3y&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.calendar.twoYear&quot;:&quot;2y&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.cumulative&quot;:&quot;Cumulative&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.cumulative.fiveYear&quot;:&quot;5y&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.cumulative.inception&quot;:&quot;Incept.&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.cumulative.missingData&quot;:&quot;Missing cumulative returns data&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.cumulative.oneMonth&quot;:&quot;1m&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.cumulative.oneYear&quot;:&quot;1y&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.cumulative.sixMonth&quot;:&quot;6m&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.cumulative.tenYear&quot;:&quot;10y&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.cumulative.threeMonth&quot;:&quot;3m&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.cumulative.threeYear&quot;:&quot;3y&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.cumulative.twoYear&quot;:&quot;2y&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.cumulative.yearToDate&quot;:&quot;YTD&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.discrete&quot;:&quot;Discrete&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.discrete.fiveYear&quot;:&quot;{0}&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.discrete.fourYear&quot;:&quot;{0}&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.discrete.missingData&quot;:&quot;Performance is not shown as the product has a performance history of less than 1 year&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.discrete.oneYear&quot;:&quot;{0}&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.discrete.threeYear&quot;:&quot;{0}&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.discrete.twoYear&quot;:&quot;{0}&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.fundDiscreteQuarterEnd&quot;:&quot;Total Return (%)&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.fundVolatility&quot;:&quot;Standard Deviation (%)&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.historical-prefix&quot;:&quot;Historical&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.levelCalced&quot;:&quot;Benchmark (%)&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.lipperDenominator&quot;:&quot;Lipper Denominator (%)&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.lipperMktDnr&quot;:&quot;Lipper Market DNR (%)&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.lipperMktNmr&quot;:&quot;Lipper Market NMR (%)&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.lipperNumerator&quot;:&quot;Lipper Numerator (%)&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.lipperRanking&quot;:&quot;Lipper Ranking&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.marketPrice&quot;:&quot;Market Price (%)&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.missingData&quot;:&quot;Returns data not available for display.&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.morningstarPerf&quot;:&quot;Total Return (%)&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.morningstarRank&quot;:&quot;Morningstar Quartile&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.morningstarStandardYearly&quot;:&quot;Total Return (%)&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.navCalced&quot;:&quot;Total Return (%)&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.navSourced&quot;:&quot;Total Return (%)&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.navSourcedNet&quot;:&quot;Return w/ Sales Charge (%)&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.secBenchmarkSourced&quot;:&quot;{0}&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.secBenchmarkSourced.infobubble&quot;:&quot;{5} shown for illustrative purposes only to demonstrate how this fund has performed vs. the broader respective market.&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.secBenchmarkSourced.minVol.infobubble&quot;:&quot;{5} (“Broad Index”) shown for illustrative purposes only to demonstrate how this fund has performed vs. the broader respective market.  The Broad Index weights securities in the index based on float-adjusted market value and generally exhibits higher volatility than the minimum volatility indexes. Minimum volatility indexes utilize a rules-based methodology in an effort to construct a portfolio of lowest absolute volatility. For international exposures, more countries may be represented in the broad index.&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.secBenchmarkSourced.multiFact.infobubble&quot;:&quot;{5} (“Broad Index”) shown for illustrative purposes only to demonstrate how this fund has performed vs. the broader respective market.  The Broad Index weights securities in the index based on float-adjusted market value. The Multifactor index utilize a rules-based methodology, weighted to provide a high level of four investment style factors.  For international exposures, more countries may be represented in the Broad Index.&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.secBenchmarkYearlySourced&quot;:&quot;{0}&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.secBenchmarkYearlySourced.infobubble&quot;:&quot;{5} shown for illustrative purposes only to demonstrate how this fund has performed vs. the broader respective market.&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.secBenchmarkYearlySourced.minVol.infobubble&quot;:&quot;{5} (“Broad Index”) shown for illustrative purposes only to demonstrate how this fund has performed vs. the broader respective market.  The Broad Index weights securities in the index based on float-adjusted market value and generally exhibits higher volatility than the minimum volatility indexes. Minimum volatility indexes utilize a rules-based methodology in an effort to construct a portfolio of lowest absolute volatility. For international exposures, more countries may be represented in the broad index.&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.secBenchmarkYearlySourced.multiFact.infobubble&quot;:&quot;{5} (“Broad Index”) shown for illustrative purposes only to demonstrate how this fund has performed vs. the broader respective market.  The Broad Index weights securities in the index based on float-adjusted market value. The Multifactor index utilize a rules-based methodology, weighted to provide a high level of four investment style factors.  For international exposures, more countries may be represented in the Broad Index.&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.standardYearlyNet&quot;:&quot;Annual w/ Sales Charge (%)&quot;,&quot;performance.returns.volatilitySourced&quot;:&quot;Standard Deviation (%)&quot;,&quot;performance.returnsCalendarChart.bmHatchingDateInfo&quot;:&quot;*Prior to {0}, the Fund used a different benchmark which is reflected in the benchmark data.&quot;,&quot;performance.returnsCalendarChart.fundHatchingDateInfo&quot;:&quot;*On {0}, the Fund changed its name and/or investment objective and policy.&quot;,&quot;performance.returnsCalendarChart.upper-diclaimer&quot;:&quot;This chart shows the product&amp;#39;s performance as the percentage loss or gain per year over the last {0} years.&quot;,&quot;performance.returnsCalendarChart.upper-diclaimer.with-bm&quot;:&quot;This chart shows the product’s performance as the percentage loss or gain per year over the last {0} years against its benchmark. It can help you to assess how the product has been managed in the past and compare it to its benchmark.&quot;,&quot;performance.tab.distributions&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;performance.tab.hypothetical&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;performance.tab.premiumDiscount&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;performance.tab.returns&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;performance.title&quot;:&quot;Performance&quot;,&quot;premium-discount-chart.chart.description.infobubble&quot;:&quot;The above table and line graph present information about the differences between the daily closing price for shares of the fund and the fund’s net asset value.  The closing prices are determined by the fund’s listing exchange.  The vertical axis of the line graph shows the premium or discount expressed as a percentage of NAV.  The horizontal axis indicates the date at which the premium/discount occurred.  The table shows the number of trading days in which the fund traded at a premium, discount or at NAV.&quot;,&quot;premium-discount-chart.chart.timing.infobubble&quot;:&quot;Note on international funds:  The premiums and discount shown for international funds may be less accurate due to the differences in closing times between U.S. and international markets.  NAVs for most International funds are calculated by using closing securities prices from local markets and the Reuters/WM FX rates at 4:00 PM London Time.  Therefore, during the second part of the U.S. trading day, the NAVs for most international funds are frozen, yet the market prices for these funds continue to fluctuate to reflect new information.  As a result, for most international funds, the traditional measure of premium/discount (closing price/NAV) may be more reflective of different market hours than true trading premium/discounts.&quot;,&quot;premium-discount-chart.table.discount.infobubble&quot;:&quot;Number of trading days the ETF’s closing price is below the NAV.&quot;,&quot;premium-discount-chart.table.nav.infobubble&quot;:&quot;NAV is the price per share in which each fund issues and redeems shares.  It is calculated by the fund accountants in accordance with the standard formula for valuing mutual fund shares at the close of regular trading (normally 4:00 PM ET) every day the New York Stock Exchange is open.&quot;,&quot;premium-discount-chart.table.premium.infobubble&quot;:&quot;Number of trading days the ETF’s closing price exceeds its NAV.&quot;,&quot;premiumDiscount.description.infobubble&quot;:&quot;The above chart presents information about the difference between the daily market price for shares of the Fund and the Fund&amp;#39;s net asset value. The market price is determined using the midpoint between the highest bid and the lowest offer on the listing exchange, as of the time that the Fund&amp;#39;s NAV is calculated (usually 4:00 p.m. eastern time for most iShares Funds). The vertical axis of the chart shows the premium or discount expressed as a percentage of NAV. The horizontal axis indicates the number of trading days in the period covered by the chart.  Each bar in the chart shows the number of trading days in which the Fund traded within the premium/discount range indicated. IMPORTANT NOTE:  The horizontal bar for ≥ 0.0 up to 0.5 includes the days that the Fund’s market price matched its NAV (that is, there was no premium or discount so the &amp;quot;premium/discount&amp;quot; percentage equaled zero.)&quot;,&quot;premiumDiscount.discount.infobubble&quot;:&quot;The lowest amount the Fund traded below the reported NAV during the period.&quot;,&quot;premiumDiscount.navAmount.infobubble&quot;:&quot;NAV is the price per share at which each fund issues and redeems shares. It is calculated by the fund accountants in accordance with the standard formula for valuing mutual fund shares at the close of regular trading (normally 4:00 p.m. eastern time) every day the New York Stock Exchange is open.&quot;,&quot;premiumDiscount.premium.infobubble&quot;:&quot;The highest amount the Fund traded above the reported NAV during the period.&quot;,&quot;premiumDiscount.timing.infobubble&quot;:&quot;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;Close of Trading Times: The NAV of BlackRock funds normally is calculated using prices as of 4:00 p.m. eastern time. Each BlackRock Fund normally trades on its respective stock exchange until 4:00 p.m. eastern time.&amp;lt;/p&amp;gt;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;Time of Last Trade: Trading generally takes place throughout the normal trading hours for BlackRock Funds on the listing exchange on which it is listed (generally 9:30 a.m. - 4:00 p.m. eastern time). At times, many trades are placed in rapid succession. At other times, little or no trading activity is taking place. It is important to note that the date/time of the last trade (which is recorded as the Closing Price) may not take place at exactly 4:00 p.m. eastern time when the BlackRock funds normally calculate NAV. The date/time of the last trade sometimes may occur before 4:00 p.m. eastern time. Thus, ongoing price discovery may result in a deviation between the price recorded as the Closing Price and the NAV of the fund shares calculated at 4:00 p.m. eastern time.&amp;lt;/p&amp;gt;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;Note on international funds: The premiums and discounts shown for international funds may be less accurate due to the difference in closing times between US and international markets. NAVs for most international BlackRock funds are calculated by using closing securities prices from local markets and Reuters/WM FX rates at 4 p.m. London time. Therefore, during the second part of the US trading day, the NAVs for most international BlackRock Funds are frozen, yet the market prices for these funds continue to fluctuate to reflect new information. As a result, for most international BlackRock Funds, the traditional measure of premium/discount (market price / NAV) may be more reflective of different market hours than true trading premium/discounts.&amp;lt;/p&amp;gt;&quot;,&quot;sr-only.pdf-tab&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;literature.seeAllDocuments&quot;:&quot;See all documents&quot;,&quot;literature.title&quot;:&quot;Literature&quot;,&quot;literature.title.v3&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;productLiteraturePalette.title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;lipper-cons-ret.infobubble&quot;:&quot;{0} received the following Consistent Return ratings for the 3-, 5-, and 10-year periods, respectively: {8} ({5} funds), {9} ({6} funds), and {10} ({7} funds).&amp;lt;br /&amp;gt;&amp;lt;br /&amp;gt;Lipper ratings for Consistent Return reflect funds&amp;#39; historical risk-adjusted returns, adjusted for volatility, relative to peers.&quot;,&quot;lipper-expense.infobubble&quot;:&quot;{0} received the following Expense ratings for the 3-, 5-, and 10-year periods, respectively: {29} ({26} funds), {30} ({27} funds), and {31} ({28} funds).&amp;lt;br /&amp;gt;&amp;lt;br /&amp;gt;Lipper ratings for Expense reflect funds&amp;#39; expense minimization relative to peers with similar load structures.&quot;,&quot;lipper-preservation.infobubble&quot;:&quot;{0} received the following Preservation ratings for the 3-, 5-, and 10-year periods, respectively: {15} ({12} funds), {16} ({13} funds), and {17} ({14} funds).&amp;lt;br /&amp;gt;&amp;lt;br /&amp;gt;Lipper ratings for Preservation reflect funds&amp;#39; historical loss avoidance relative to other funds within the same asset class. Preservation ratings are relative, rather than absolute, measures, and funds named Lipper Leaders for Preservation may still experience losses periodically; those losses may be larger for equity and mixed equity funds than for fixed income funds.&quot;,&quot;lipper-tax-eff.infobubble&quot;:&quot;{0} received the following Tax Efficiency ratings for the 3-, 5-, and 10-year periods, respectively: {36} ({33} funds), {37} ({34} funds), and {38} ({35} funds).&amp;lt;br /&amp;gt;&amp;lt;br /&amp;gt;Lipper ratings for Tax Efficiency (US) reflect funds&amp;#39; historical success in postponing taxable distributions relative to peers. Tax Efficiency (US) offers no benefit to investors in tax-sheltered accounts such as retirement plans.&quot;,&quot;lipper-tot-ret.infobubble&quot;:&quot;{0} received the following Total Return ratings for the 3-, 5-, and 10-year periods, respectively: {22} ({19} funds), {23} ({20} funds), and {24} ({21} funds).&amp;lt;br /&amp;gt;&amp;lt;br /&amp;gt;Lipper ratings for Total Return reflect funds&amp;#39; historical total return performance relative to peers.&quot;,&quot;ratingsAndAwards.lipper.disclaimer&quot;:&quot;Overall Lipper Leaders ratings based on an equal-weighted average of percentile ranks for each measure over 3-, 5-, and 10-year periods (if applicable) and do not take into account the effects of sales charges for these categories (Consistent Return, Preservation, Total Return, Expense, and Tax Efficiency) as of {2} out of {4}, {11}, {18}, {25} and {32} Funds, respectively in Lipper&amp;#39;s {3} classification.&quot;,&quot;ratingsAndAwards.lipper.heading&quot;:&quot;Lipper Leader&quot;,&quot;ratingsAndAwards.lipper.lipper-cons-ret&quot;:&quot;Consistent Return&quot;,&quot;ratingsAndAwards.lipper.lipper-expense&quot;:&quot;Expense&quot;,&quot;ratingsAndAwards.lipper.lipper-preservation&quot;:&quot;Preservation&quot;,&quot;ratingsAndAwards.lipper.lipper-tax-eff&quot;:&quot;Tax Efficiency&quot;,&quot;ratingsAndAwards.lipper.lipper-tot-ret&quot;:&quot;Total Return&quot;,&quot;ratingsAndAwards.lipper.title&quot;:&quot;Lipper Leader Ratings&quot;,&quot;ratingsAndAwards.mstarAnalystDrivenPct.title&quot;:&quot;Analyst-Driven %&quot;,&quot;ratingsAndAwards.mstarAnalystDrivenPct.title.infobubble&quot;:&quot;Analyst Driven % is the analyst input into the overall rating assignment, including direct analyst coverage and inheritance of an analyst-rated pillar&quot;,&quot;ratingsAndAwards.mstarAnalystRating.effective&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;ratingsAndAwards.mstarAnalystRating.footnote.bronze&quot;:&quot;Morningstar has awarded the Fund a Bronze medal. (Effective {0})&quot;,&quot;ratingsAndAwards.mstarAnalystRating.footnote.gold&quot;:&quot;Morningstar has awarded the Fund a Gold medal. (Effective {0})&quot;,&quot;ratingsAndAwards.mstarAnalystRating.footnote.infobubble&quot;:&quot;The Morningstar Medalist RatingTM is the summary expression of Morningstar’s forward-looking analysis of investment strategies as offered via specific vehicles using a rating scale of Gold, Silver, Bronze, Neutral, and Negative. The Medalist Ratings indicate which investments Morningstar believes are likely to outperform a relevant index or peer group average on a risk-adjusted basis over time. Investment products are evaluated on three key pillars (People, Parent, and Process) which, when coupled with a fee assessment, forms the basis for Morningstar’s conviction in those products’ investment merits and determines the Medalist Rating they’re assigned. Pillar ratings take the form of Low, Below Average, Average, Above Average, and High. Pillars may be evaluated via an analyst’s qualitative assessment (either directly to a vehicle the analyst covers or indirectly when the pillar ratings of a covered vehicle are mapped to a related uncovered vehicle) or using algorithmic techniques. Vehicles are sorted by their expected performance into rating groups defined by their Morningstar Category and their active or passive status. When analysts directly cover a vehicle, they assign the three pillar ratings based on their qualitative assessment, subject to the oversight of the Analyst Rating Committee, and monitor and reevaluate them at least every 14 months. When the vehicles are covered either indirectly by analysts or by algorithm, the ratings are assigned monthly. For more detailed information about these ratings, including their methodology, please go to global.morningstar.com/managerdisclosures/. The Morningstar Medalist Ratings are not statements of fact, nor are they credit or risk ratings. The Morningstar Medalist Rating (i) should not be used as the sole basis in evaluating an investment product, (ii) involves unknown risks and uncertainties which may cause expectations not to occur or to differ significantly from what was expected, (iii) are not guaranteed to be based on complete or accurate assumptions or models when determined algorithmically, (iv) involve the risk that the return target will not be met due to such things as unforeseen changes in management, technology, economic development, interest rate development, operating and/or material costs, competitive pressure, supervisory law, exchange rate, tax rates, exchange rate changes, and/or changes in political and social conditions, and (v) should not be considered an offer or solicitation to buy or sell the investment product. A change in the fundamental factors underlying the Morningstar Medalist Rating can mean that the rating is subsequently no longer accurate.&quot;,&quot;ratingsAndAwards.mstarAnalystRating.footnote.silver&quot;:&quot;Morningstar has awarded the Fund a Silver medal. (Effective {0})&quot;,&quot;ratingsAndAwards.mstarDataAvailabilityPct.title&quot;:&quot;Data Coverage %&quot;,&quot;ratingsAndAwards.mstarDataAvailabilityPct.title.infobubble&quot;:&quot;Data Coverage % is available input data for rating calculation at the Pillar level&quot;,&quot;ratingsAndAwards.mstarRatingOverall.infobubble&quot;:&quot;{0} received a Morningstar Rating of {5} stars for the 3-year period, {7} for the 5-year period and {9} for the 10-year period, rated against {6}, {8} and {10} {4} Funds, respectively. Performance results represent past performance and are no guarantee of future results.&amp;lt;br /&amp;gt;&amp;lt;br /&amp;gt;For each U.S.-domiciled fund with at least a 3-year history, Morningstar calculates a Morningstar RatingTM based on a Morningstar Risk-Adjusted Return measure that accounts for variation in a fund&amp;#39;s monthly performance (including the effects of sales charges, loads and redemption fees), placing more emphasis on downward variations and rewarding consistent performance. The top 10% of funds in each category receive five stars, the next 22.5% receive four stars, the next 35% receive three stars, the next 22.5% receive two stars and the bottom 10% receive one star. (Each share class is counted as a fraction of one fund within this scale and rated separately, which may cause slight variations in the distribution percentages.) The Overall Morningstar Rating for a fund is derived from a weighted-average of the performance figures associated with its 3-, 5- and 10-year (if applicable) Morningstar Rating metrics.&amp;lt;br /&amp;gt;&amp;lt;br /&amp;gt;Morningstar Ratings are for the share classes cited only; other classes may have different ratings.&quot;,&quot;ratingsAndAwards.mstarRatingOverall.notAvailable&quot;:&quot;no rating was provided&quot;,&quot;ratingsAndAwards.mstarRatingOverall.title&quot;:&quot;Morningstar Rating&quot;,&quot;ratingsAndAwards.title&quot;:&quot;Ratings&quot;,&quot;registeredCountries.title&quot;:&quot;Registered Locations&quot;,&quot;download.collateralSnapshot&quot;:&quot;Download Collateral Snapshot&quot;,&quot;secLending.collateral-matrix&quot;:&quot;Collateral Matrix&quot;,&quot;secLending.collateral-snapshot&quot;:&quot;Collateral Snapshot&quot;,&quot;secLending.collateral-snapshot.assetClass&quot;:&quot;Asset Class&quot;,&quot;secLending.collateral-snapshot.countryOfRisk&quot;:&quot;Location&quot;,&quot;secLending.collateral-snapshot.exchange&quot;:&quot;Exchange&quot;,&quot;secLending.collateral-snapshot.filterInput&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;secLending.collateral-snapshot.holdingPercent&quot;:&quot;Weight %&quot;,&quot;secLending.collateral-snapshot.isin&quot;:&quot;ISIN&quot;,&quot;secLending.collateral-snapshot.issueName&quot;:&quot;Name&quot;,&quot;secLending.collateral-snapshot.notionalValue&quot;:&quot;Notional Value&quot;,&quot;secLending.collateral-snapshot.sedol&quot;:&quot;SEDOL&quot;,&quot;secLending.collateral-snapshot.ticker&quot;:&quot;Ticker&quot;,&quot;secLending.download.asOfDate&quot;:&quot;Collateral Snapshot as of&quot;,&quot;secLending.download.assetClass&quot;:&quot;Asset Class&quot;,&quot;secLending.download.countryOfRisk&quot;:&quot;Country&quot;,&quot;secLending.download.exchange&quot;:&quot;Exchange&quot;,&quot;secLending.download.holdingPercent&quot;:&quot;Weight %&quot;,&quot;secLending.download.isin&quot;:&quot;ISIN&quot;,&quot;secLending.download.issueName&quot;:&quot;Name&quot;,&quot;secLending.download.notionalValue&quot;:&quot;Notional Value&quot;,&quot;secLending.download.sedol&quot;:&quot;SEDOL&quot;,&quot;secLending.download.ticker&quot;:&quot;Ticker&quot;,&quot;secLending.summary&quot;:&quot;Lending Summary&quot;,&quot;secLending.summary.avgCollateralisation&quot;:&quot;Collateralisation (% of Loan)&quot;,&quot;secLending.summary.avgCollateralisation.infobubble&quot;:&quot;Average value of collateral as a percentage of on loan value throughout the period.&quot;,&quot;secLending.summary.avgOnLoan&quot;:&quot;Average on-loan (% of AUM)&quot;,&quot;secLending.summary.avgOnLoan.infobubble&quot;:&quot;Average on loan value as a percentage of the average AUM of the fund throughout the period.&quot;,&quot;secLending.summary.fiveYear&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;secLending.summary.fourYear&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;secLending.summary.from&quot;:&quot;From&quot;,&quot;secLending.summary.maxOnLoan&quot;:&quot;Maximum on-loan (% of AUM)&quot;,&quot;secLending.summary.maxOnLoan.infobubble&quot;:&quot;Maximum on loan values as a percentage of the AUM of the fund throught the period.&quot;,&quot;secLending.summary.missingData&quot;:&quot;Sorry, no Lending Summary data available.&quot;,&quot;secLending.summary.netSecLendingPerf&quot;:&quot;Securities Lending Return (%)&quot;,&quot;secLending.summary.netSecLendingPerf.infobubble&quot;:&quot;Securities Lending Return is calculated using unaudited 12 month net securities lending revenues to the fund divided by the average NAV of the fund over the same period. 62.5% of all securities lending income is paid directly into the fund, with BlackRock receiving 37.5% compensation which covers all operational costs. &quot;,&quot;secLending.summary.oneYear&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;secLending.summary.threeYear&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;secLending.summary.to&quot;:&quot;To&quot;,&quot;secLending.summary.twoYear&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;secLending.summeryOneYearRule.missingData&quot;:&quot;Lending Summary not available as there is less than one year&amp;#39;s performance data&quot;,&quot;secLending.title&quot;:&quot;Securities Lending&quot;,&quot;sfdr.title&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;content&quot;:{&quot;amc-disclaimer&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Ongoing Charge may be discounted depending on the size of the fund.&quot;}],&quot;audience-message-insti&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;&lt;strong&gt;This document is marketing material. For Investors in the UK. Defined Contribution. THI