uot;:&quot;&lt;p&gt;ESG integration is the practice of incorporating material environmental, social and governance (ESG) information or insights alongside traditional measures into the investment decision process to improve long term financial outcomes of portfolios. &lt;strong&gt;Unless otherwise stated in Fund documentation or included within the Fund’s investment objective, inclusion of this statement does not imply that the Fund has an ESG-aligned investment objective, but rather describes how ESG information is considered as part of the overall investment process.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;br /&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;The Fund manager designs research, portfolio construction, and decision phases of the investment process to reflect emphasis on relevant, internal ESG research related to assessments of certain characteristics, including, but not limited to, economic and environmental transition, market structure, superior growth, management quality, and risk characteristics associated with environmental, social, and governance matters. ESG insights are combined with other internal research views to achieve active portfolio weighting versus a reference benchmark (or weighting implemented to achieve an absolute return outcome in portfolios without a benchmark) which considers the portfolio’s ESG mandate.  The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion of the portfolio’s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate metrics, and other factors.&lt;/p&gt;&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-55&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Fund manager may include ESG considerations in the research and decision phases of the investment process. Funds with ESG-related objectives may also include ESG considerations in the portfolio construction phase of the investment process. The research phase may include relevant, internal ESG research used to assess certain characteristics, including, but not limited to, economic and environmental transition, market structure, superior growth, management quality, and risk characteristics associated with environmental, social, and governance matters. ESG insights may be combined with other internal research views to inform active portfolio weighting versus a reference benchmark (or weighting implemented to achieve an absolute return outcome, if applicable). The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion, where appropriate, of the portfolio&#x27;s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate metrics, and other factors.&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-55BROAD&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;&lt;p&gt;ESG integration is the practice of incorporating material environmental, social and governance (ESG) information or insights alongside traditional measures into the investment decision process to improve long term financial outcomes of portfolios. &lt;strong&gt;Unless otherwise stated in Fund documentation or included within the Fund’s investment objective, inclusion of this statement does not imply that the Fund has an ESG-aligned investment objective, but rather describes how ESG information is considered as part of the overall investment process.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;br /&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;The Fund manager designs research, portfolio construction, and decision phases of the investment process to reflect emphasis on relevant, internal ESG research related to assessments of certain characteristics, including, but not limited to, economic and environmental transition, market structure, superior growth, management quality, and risk characteristics associated with environmental, social, and governance matters. ESG insights are combined with other internal research views to achieve active portfolio weighting versus a reference benchmark (or weighting implemented to achieve an absolute return outcome in portfolios without a benchmark) which considers the portfolio’s ESG mandate.  The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion of the portfolio’s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate metrics, and other factors.&lt;/p&gt;&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-55IMPACT&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;&lt;p&gt;ESG integration is the practice of incorporating material environmental, social and governance (ESG) information or insights alongside traditional measures into the investment decision process to improve long term financial outcomes of portfolios. &lt;strong&gt;Unless otherwise stated in Fund documentation or included within the Fund’s investment objective, inclusion of this statement does not imply that the Fund has an ESG-aligned investment objective, but rather describes how ESG information is considered as part of the overall investment process.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;br /&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;The Fund manager designs research, portfolio construction, and decision phases of the investment process to reflect emphasis on relevant, internal ESG research related to assessments of certain characteristics, including, but not limited to, economic and environmental transition, market structure, superior growth, management quality, and risk characteristics associated with environmental, social, and governance matters. ESG insights are combined with other internal research views to achieve active portfolio weighting versus a reference benchmark (or weighting implemented to achieve an absolute return outcome in portfolios without a benchmark) which considers the portfolio’s ESG mandate.  The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion of the portfolio’s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate metrics, and other factors.&lt;/p&gt;&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-55SCREEN&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;&lt;p&gt;ESG integration is the practice of incorporating material environmental, social and governance (ESG) information or insights alongside traditional measures into the investment decision process to improve long term financial outcomes of portfolios. &lt;strong&gt;Unless otherwise stated in Fund documentation or included within the Fund’s investment objective, inclusion of this statement does not imply that the Fund has an ESG-aligned investment objective, but rather describes how ESG information is considered as part of the overall investment process.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;br /&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;The Fund manager designs research, portfolio construction, and decision phases of the investment process to reflect emphasis on relevant, internal ESG research related to assessments of certain characteristics, including, but not limited to, economic and environmental transition, market structure, superior growth, management quality, and risk characteristics associated with environmental, social, and governance matters. ESG insights are combined with other internal research views to achieve active portfolio weighting versus a reference benchmark (or weighting implemented to achieve an absolute return outcome in portfolios without a benchmark) which considers the portfolio’s ESG mandate.  The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion of the portfolio’s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate metrics, and other factors.&lt;/p&gt;&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-55THEMATIC&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;&lt;p&gt;ESG integration is the practice of incorporating material environmental, social and governance (ESG) information or insights alongside traditional measures into the investment decision process to improve long term financial outcomes of portfolios. &lt;strong&gt;Unless otherwise stated in Fund documentation or included within the Fund’s investment objective, inclusion of this statement does not imply that the Fund has an ESG-aligned investment objective, but rather describes how ESG information is considered as part of the overall investment process.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;br /&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;The Fund manager designs research, portfolio construction, and decision phases of the investment process to reflect emphasis on relevant, internal ESG research related to assessments of certain characteristics, including, but not limited to, economic and environmental transition, market structure, superior growth, management quality, and risk characteristics associated with environmental, social, and governance matters. ESG insights are combined with other internal research views to achieve active portfolio weighting versus a reference benchmark (or weighting implemented to achieve an absolute return outcome in portfolios without a benchmark) which considers the portfolio’s ESG mandate.  The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion of the portfolio’s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate metrics, and other factors.&lt;/p&gt;&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-55UPLIFT&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;&lt;p&gt;ESG integration is the practice of incorporating material environmental, social and governance (ESG) information or insights alongside traditional measures into the investment decision process to improve long term financial outcomes of portfolios. &lt;strong&gt;Unless otherwise stated in Fund documentation or included within the Fund’s investment objective, inclusion of this statement does not imply that the Fund has an ESG-aligned investment objective, but rather describes how ESG information is considered as part of the overall investment process.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;br /&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;The Fund manager designs research, portfolio construction, and decision phases of the investment process to reflect emphasis on relevant, internal ESG research related to assessments of certain characteristics, including, but not limited to, economic and environmental transition, market structure, superior growth, management quality, and risk characteristics associated with environmental, social, and governance matters. ESG insights are combined with other internal research views to achieve active portfolio weighting versus a reference benchmark (or weighting implemented to achieve an absolute return outcome in portfolios without a benchmark) which considers the portfolio’s ESG mandate.  The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion of the portfolio’s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate metrics, and other factors.&lt;/p&gt;&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-56&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Fund manager may include ESG considerations in the research and decision phases of the investment process. Funds with ESG-related objectives may also include ESG considerations in the portfolio construction phase of the investment process. The research phase may include relevant, internal ESG research used to assess certain characteristics, including, but not limited to, economic and environmental transition, market structure, superior growth, management quality, and risk characteristics associated with environmental, social, and governance matters. ESG insights may be combined with other internal research views to inform active portfolio weighting versus a reference benchmark (or weighting implemented to achieve an absolute return outcome, if applicable). The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion, where appropriate, of the portfolio&#x27;s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate metrics, and other factors.&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-56BROAD&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;&lt;p&gt;ESG integration is the practice of incorporating material environmental, social and governance (ESG) information or insights alongside traditional measures into the investment decision process to improve long term financial outcomes of portfolios. &lt;strong&gt;Unless otherwise stated in Fund documentation or included within the Fund’s investment objective, inclusion of this statement does not imply that the Fund has an ESG-aligned investment objective, but rather describes how ESG information is considered as part of the overall investment process.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;br /&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;The Fund manager designs research, portfolio construction, and decision phases of the investment process to reflect emphasis on relevant, internal ESG research related to assessments of certain characteristics, including, but not limited to, economic and environmental transition, market structure, superior growth, management quality, and risk characteristics associated with environmental, social, and governance matters. ESG insights are combined with other internal research views to achieve active portfolio weighting versus a reference benchmark (or weighting implemented to achieve an absolute return outcome in portfolios without a benchmark) which considers the portfolio’s ESG mandate.  The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion of the portfolio’s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate metrics, and other factors.&lt;/p&gt;&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-56IMPACT&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;&lt;p&gt;ESG integration is the practice of incorporating material environmental, social and governance (ESG) information or insights alongside traditional measures into the investment decision process to improve long term financial outcomes of portfolios. &lt;strong&gt;Unless otherwise stated in Fund documentation or included within the Fund’s investment objective, inclusion of this statement does not imply that the Fund has an ESG-aligned investment objective, but rather describes how ESG information is considered as part of the overall investment process.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;br /&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;The Fund manager designs research, portfolio construction, and decision phases of the investment process to reflect emphasis on relevant, internal ESG research related to assessments of certain characteristics, including, but not limited to, economic and environmental transition, market structure, superior growth, management quality, and risk characteristics associated with environmental, social, and governance matters. ESG insights are combined with other internal research views to achieve active portfolio weighting versus a reference benchmark (or weighting implemented to achieve an absolute return outcome in portfolios without a benchmark) which considers the portfolio’s ESG mandate.  The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion of the portfolio’s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate metrics, and other factors.&lt;/p&gt;&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-56SCREEN&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;&lt;p&gt;ESG integration is the practice of incorporating material environmental, social and governance (ESG) information or insights alongside traditional measures into the investment decision process to improve long term financial outcomes of portfolios. &lt;strong&gt;Unless otherwise stated in Fund documentation or included within the Fund’s investment objective, inclusion of this statement does not imply that the Fund has an ESG-aligned investment objective, but rather describes how ESG information is considered as part of the overall investment process.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;br /&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;The Fund manager designs research, portfolio construction, and decision phases of the investment process to reflect emphasis on relevant, internal ESG research related to assessments of certain characteristics, including, but not limited to, economic and environmental transition, market structure, superior growth, management quality, and risk characteristics associated with environmental, social, and governance matters. ESG insights are combined with other internal research views to achieve active portfolio weighting versus a reference benchmark (or weighting implemented to achieve an absolute return outcome in portfolios without a benchmark) which considers the portfolio’s ESG mandate.  The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion of the portfolio’s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate metrics, and other factors.&lt;/p&gt;&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-56THEMATIC&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;&lt;p&gt;ESG integration is the practice of incorporating material environmental, social and governance (ESG) information or insights alongside traditional measures into the investment decision process to improve long term financial outcomes of portfolios. &lt;strong&gt;Unless otherwise stated in Fund documentation or included within the Fund’s investment objective, inclusion of this statement does not imply that the Fund has an ESG-aligned investment objective, but rather describes how ESG information is considered as part of the overall investment process.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;br /&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;The Fund manager designs research, portfolio construction, and decision phases of the investment process to reflect emphasis on relevant, internal ESG research related to assessments of certain characteristics, including, but not limited to, economic and environmental transition, market structure, superior growth, management quality, and risk characteristics associated with environmental, social, and governance matters. ESG insights are combined with other internal research views to achieve active portfolio weighting versus a reference benchmark (or weighting implemented to achieve an absolute return outcome in portfolios without a benchmark) which considers the portfolio’s ESG mandate.  The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion of the portfolio’s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate metrics, and other factors.&lt;/p&gt;&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-56UPLIFT&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;&lt;p&gt;ESG integration is the practice of incorporating material environmental, social and governance (ESG) information or insights alongside traditional measures into the investment decision process to improve long term financial outcomes of portfolios. &lt;strong&gt;Unless otherwise stated in Fund documentation or included within the Fund’s investment objective, inclusion of this statement does not imply that the Fund has an ESG-aligned investment objective, but rather describes how ESG information is considered as part of the overall investment process.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;br /&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;The Fund manager designs research, portfolio construction, and decision phases of the investment process to reflect emphasis on relevant, internal ESG research related to assessments of certain characteristics, including, but not limited to, economic and environmental transition, market structure, superior growth, management quality, and risk characteristics associated with environmental, social, and governance matters. ESG insights are combined with other internal research views to achieve active portfolio weighting versus a reference benchmark (or weighting implemented to achieve an absolute return outcome in portfolios without a benchmark) which considers the portfolio’s ESG mandate.  The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion of the portfolio’s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate metrics, and other factors.&lt;/p&gt;&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-58&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Fund manager may include ESG considerations in the research and decision phases of the investment process. Funds with ESG-related objectives may also include ESG considerations in the portfolio construction phase of the investment process. The research phase may include relevant, internal ESG research used to assess certain characteristics, including, but not limited to, economic and environmental transition, market structure, superior growth, management quality, and risk characteristics associated with environmental, social, and governance matters. ESG insights may be combined with other internal research views to inform active portfolio weighting versus a reference benchmark (or weighting implemented to achieve an absolute return outcome, if applicable). The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion, where appropriate, of the portfolio&#x27;s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate metrics, and other factors.&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-58BROAD&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;&lt;p&gt;ESG integration is the practice of incorporating material environmental, social and governance (ESG) information or insights alongside traditional measures into the investment decision process to improve long term financial outcomes of portfolios. &lt;strong&gt;Unless otherwise stated in Fund documentation or included within the Fund’s investment objective, inclusion of this statement does not imply that the Fund has an ESG-aligned investment objective, but rather describes how ESG information is considered as part of the overall investment process.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;br /&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;The Fund manager designs research, portfolio construction, and decision phases of the investment process to reflect emphasis on relevant, internal ESG research related to assessments of certain characteristics, including, but not limited to, economic and environmental transition, market structure, superior growth, management quality, and risk characteristics associated with environmental, social, and governance matters. ESG insights are combined with other internal research views to achieve active portfolio weighting versus a reference benchmark (or weighting implemented to achieve an absolute return outcome in portfolios without a benchmark) which considers the portfolio’s ESG mandate.  The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion of the portfolio’s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate metrics, and other factors.&lt;/p&gt;&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-58IMPACT&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;&lt;p&gt;ESG integration is the practice of incorporating material environmental, social and governance (ESG) information or insights alongside traditional measures into the investment decision process to improve long term financial outcomes of portfolios. &lt;strong&gt;Unless otherwise stated in Fund documentation or included within the Fund’s investment objective, inclusion of this statement does not imply that the Fund has an ESG-aligned investment objective, but rather describes how ESG information is considered as part of the overall investment process.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;br /&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;The Fund manager designs research, portfolio construction, and decision phases of the investment process to reflect emphasis on relevant, internal ESG research related to assessments of certain characteristics, including, but not limited to, economic and environmental transition, market structure, superior growth, management quality, and risk characteristics associated with environmental, social, and governance matters. ESG insights are combined with other internal research views to achieve active portfolio weighting versus a reference benchmark (or weighting implemented to achieve an absolute return outcome in portfolios without a benchmark) which considers the portfolio’s ESG mandate.  The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion of the portfolio’s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate metrics, and other factors.&lt;/p&gt;&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-58SCREEN&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;&lt;p&gt;ESG integration is the practice of incorporating material environmental, social and governance (ESG) information or insights alongside traditional measures into the investment decision process to improve long term financial outcomes of portfolios. &lt;strong&gt;Unless otherwise stated in Fund documentation or included within the Fund’s investment objective, inclusion of this statement does not imply that the Fund has an ESG-aligned investment objective, but rather describes how ESG information is considered as part of the overall investment process.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;br /&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;The Fund manager designs research, portfolio construction, and decision phases of the investment process to reflect emphasis on relevant, internal ESG research related to assessments of certain characteristics, including, but not limited to, economic and environmental transition, market structure, superior growth, management quality, and risk characteristics associated with environmental, social, and governance matters. ESG insights are combined with other internal research views to achieve active portfolio weighting versus a reference benchmark (or weighting implemented to achieve an absolute return outcome in portfolios without a benchmark) which considers the portfolio’s ESG mandate.  The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion of the portfolio’s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate metrics, and other factors.&lt;/p&gt;&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-58THEMATIC&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;&lt;p&gt;ESG integration is the practice of incorporating material environmental, social and governance (ESG) information or insights alongside traditional measures into the investment decision process to improve long term financial outcomes of portfolios. &lt;strong&gt;Unless otherwise stated in Fund documentation or included within the Fund’s investment objective, inclusion of this statement does not imply that the Fund has an ESG-aligned investment objective, but rather describes how ESG information is considered as part of the overall investment process.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;br /&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;The Fund manager designs research, portfolio construction, and decision phases of the investment process to reflect emphasis on relevant, internal ESG research related to assessments of certain characteristics, including, but not limited to, economic and environmental transition, market structure, superior growth, management quality, and risk characteristics associated with environmental, social, and governance matters. ESG insights are combined with other internal research views to achieve active portfolio weighting versus a reference benchmark (or weighting implemented to achieve an absolute return outcome in portfolios without a benchmark) which considers the portfolio’s ESG mandate.  The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion of the portfolio’s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate metrics, and other factors.&lt;/p&gt;&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-58UPLIFT&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;&lt;p&gt;ESG integration is the practice of incorporating material environmental, social and governance (ESG) information or insights alongside traditional measures into the investment decision process to improve long term financial outcomes of portfolios. &lt;strong&gt;Unless otherwise stated in Fund documentation or included within the Fund’s investment objective, inclusion of this statement does not imply that the Fund has an ESG-aligned investment objective, but rather describes how ESG information is considered as part of the overall investment process.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;br /&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;The Fund manager designs research, portfolio construction, and decision phases of the investment process to reflect emphasis on relevant, internal ESG research related to assessments of certain characteristics, including, but not limited to, economic and environmental transition, market structure, superior growth, management quality, and risk characteristics associated with environmental, social, and governance matters. ESG insights are combined with other internal research views to achieve active portfolio weighting versus a reference benchmark (or weighting implemented to achieve an absolute return outcome in portfolios without a benchmark) which considers the portfolio’s ESG mandate.  The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion of the portfolio’s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate metrics, and other factors.&lt;/p&gt;&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-60&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Fund manager includes ESG considerations in combination with other information in the research phase of the investment process. This may include relevant third-party insights, as well as internal engagement commentary and input from BlackRock Investment Stewardship on governance issues. The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion, where appropriate, of the portfolio&#x27;s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate-related metrics, and other factors.&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-61&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Fund manager includes ESG considerations in combination with other information in the research phase of the investment process. This may include relevant third-party insights, as well as internal engagement commentary and input from BlackRock Investment Stewardship on governance issues. The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion, where appropriate, of the portfolio&#x27;s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate-related metrics, and other factors.&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-62&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Fund manager includes ESG considerations in the investment research, portfolio construction, and investment monitoring phases of the investment process. The Fund manager maintains internal ESG scorecards for certain issuers under consideration for investment and certain existing issuers of publicly traded securities. These scorecards analyze and track internal and external research views across a range of environmental, social, and governance factors sourced from primary and third-party ESG information and research. Portfolio management teams may consider the sector and issuer ESG views and scores during portfolio construction. The Fund manager also considers ESG criteria during post-investment monitoring and conducts regular portfolio risk reviews between the investment team and BlackRock’s Risk and Quantitative Analysis group. These reviews include discussion of the portfolio&#x27;s exposure to material ESG risks, where appropriate.&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-63&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Fund manager includes ESG considerations in the investment research, portfolio construction, and investment monitoring phases of the investment process. The Fund manager maintains internal ESG scorecards for certain issuers under consideration for investment and certain existing issuers of publicly traded securities. These scorecards analyze and track internal and external research views across a range of environmental, social, and governance factors sourced from primary and third-party ESG information and research. Portfolio management teams may consider the sector and issuer ESG views and scores during portfolio construction. The Fund manager also considers ESG criteria during post-investment monitoring and conducts regular portfolio risk reviews between the investment team and BlackRock’s Risk and Quantitative Analysis group. These reviews include discussion of the portfolio&#x27;s exposure to material ESG risks, where appropriate.&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-64&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Fund manager includes ESG considerations in combination with other information in the research phase of the investment process. This may include relevant third-party insights, as well as internal engagement commentary and input from BlackRock Investment Stewardship on governance issues. The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion, where appropriate, of the portfolio&#x27;s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate-related metrics, and other factors.&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-65&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Fund manager includes ESG considerations throughout the investment process, including sourcing, screening, due diligence, decision, and portfolio monitoring. This may include documented ESG screens preventing the Fund from investing in companies that are engaged in specified excluded sectors. In the due diligence process, the investment team uses an internal ESG risk assessment to identify, analyze and document key ESG risks where appropriate. Where applicable, the Fund manager may also consider third-party ESG data vendors or specialist consultants to support due diligence or company engagement. Potential investments are assigned an ESG rating where appropriate that reflects positive ESG attributes and material ESG risks, if any. Where appropriate, identified ESG risks and relevant mitigating actions may be documented in Investment Committee materials and discussed at relevant Investment Committee meetings. ESG criteria may impact the Investment Committee’s investment decision. The Fund’s ongoing portfolio management process includes, where appropriate, the monitoring of ESG criteria over the life of an investment, and in these cases Fund managers aim to refresh portfolio company ESG ratings on a quarterly basis. Furthermore, the investment team and BlackRock’s Risk and Quantitative Analysis group analyze exposure to material ESG risks where appropriate as part of the portfolio risk review regularly.&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-67&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Fund manager includes ESG considerations in combination with other information in the research phase of the investment process. This may include relevant third-party insights, as well as internal engagement commentary and input from BlackRock Investment Stewardship on governance issues. The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion, where appropriate, of the portfolio&#x27;s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate-related metrics, and other factors.&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-68&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Fund manager includes ESG considerations in combination with other information in the research phase of the investment process. This may include relevant third-party insights, as well as internal engagement commentary and input from BlackRock Investment Stewardship on governance issues. The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion, where appropriate, of the portfolio&#x27;s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate-related metrics, and other factors.&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-69&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Fund manager includes ESG considerations in combination with other information in the research phase of the investment process. This may include relevant third-party insights, as well as internal engagement commentary and input from BlackRock Investment Stewardship on governance issues. The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion, where appropriate, of the portfolio&#x27;s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate-related metrics, and other factors.&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-70&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Fund manager includes ESG considerations in combination with other information in the research phase of the investment process. This may include relevant third-party insights, as well as internal engagement commentary and input from BlackRock Investment Stewardship on governance issues. The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion, where appropriate, of the portfolio&#x27;s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate-related metrics, and other factors.&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-71&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Fund manager includes ESG considerations in combination with other information in the research phase of the investment process. This may include relevant third-party insights, as well as internal engagement commentary and input from BlackRock Investment Stewardship on governance issues. The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion, where appropriate, of the portfolio&#x27;s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate-related metrics, and other factors.&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-72&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Fund manager includes ESG considerations in combination with other information in the research phase of the investment process. This may include relevant third-party insights, as well as internal engagement commentary and input from BlackRock Investment Stewardship on governance issues. The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion, where appropriate, of the portfolio&#x27;s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate-related metrics, and other factors.&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-73&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Fund manager includes ESG considerations in combination with other information in the research phase of the investment process. This may include relevant third-party insights, as well as internal engagement commentary and input from BlackRock Investment Stewardship on governance issues. The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion, where appropriate, of the portfolio&#x27;s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate-related metrics, and other factors.&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-74&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Fund manager includes ESG considerations in combination with other information in the research and due diligence stage of the investment process. The Fund manager has developed internal research signals to help evaluate corporate issuers on climate, governance and human capital issues. ESG information may be sourced from both internal and external sources. The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio risk reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group. These reviews include discussion, where appropriate, of the portfolio&#x27;s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate-related metrics, and other factors.&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-77&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Fund manager includes ESG considerations in combination with other information in the research phase of the investment process. This may include relevant third-party insights, as well as internal engagement commentary and input from BlackRock Investment Stewardship on governance issues. The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion, where appropriate, of the portfolio&#x27;s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate-related metrics, and other factors.&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-78&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Fund manager includes ESG considerations in combination with other information in the research phase of the investment process. This may include relevant third-party insights, as well as internal engagement commentary and input from BlackRock Investment Stewardship on governance issues. The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion, where appropriate, of the portfolio&#x27;s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate-related metrics, and other factors.&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-79&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Fund manager includes ESG considerations in combination with other information in the research phase of the investment process. This may include relevant third-party insights, as well as internal engagement commentary and input from BlackRock Investment Stewardship on governance issues. The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion, where appropriate, of the portfolio&#x27;s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate-related metrics, and other factors.&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-80&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Fund manager includes ESG considerations in combination with other information in the research phase of the investment process. This may include relevant third-party insights, as well as internal engagement commentary and input from BlackRock Investment Stewardship on governance issues. The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion, where appropriate, of the portfolio&#x27;s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate-related metrics, and other factors.&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-81&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Where applicable, the Fund manager includes ESG considerations in combination with other information in the research and due diligence stage of the investment process. ESG information may be sourced from both internal and external sources and included in the Aladdin risk system. This information may broadly inform investment decisions: ESG criteria are considered in combination with other information. The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio risk reviews between the investment team and BlackRock&#x27;s Risk and Quantitative Analysis group. These reviews include discussion of the portfolio&#x27;s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate-related metrics, and other factors, where appropriate.&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-82&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Where applicable, the Fund manager includes ESG considerations in combination with other information in the research and due diligence stage of the investment process. ESG information may be sourced from both internal and external sources and included in the Aladdin risk system. This information may broadly inform investment decisions: ESG criteria are considered in combination with other information. The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio risk reviews between the investment team and BlackRock&#x27;s Risk and Quantitative Analysis group. These reviews include discussion of the portfolio&#x27;s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate-related metrics, and other factors, where appropriate.&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-83&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Where applicable, the Fund manager includes ESG considerations in combination with other information in the research and due diligence stage of the investment process. ESG information may be sourced from both internal and external sources and included in the Aladdin risk system. This information may broadly inform investment decisions: ESG criteria are considered in combination with other information. The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio risk reviews between the investment team and BlackRock&#x27;s Risk and Quantitative Analysis group. These reviews include discussion of the portfolio&#x27;s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate-related metrics, and other factors, where appropriate.&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-84&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Fund manager includes ESG considerations in combination with other information in the research phase of the investment process. This may include relevant third-party insights, as well as internal engagement commentary and input from BlackRock Investment Stewardship on governance issues. The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion, where appropriate, of the portfolio&#x27;s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate-related metrics, and other factors.&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-87&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Fund manager includes ESG considerations in combination with other information during the investment process. In the initial idea generation and credit research process this may include an assessment of each company&#x27;s positive ESG attributes or material risks or the use of internal sovereign or corporate ESG due diligence templates alongside third-party ESG data. Positive ESG attributes and material ESG risks and their potential financial impact are generally highlighted in credit research reports and may influence investment decisions and security selection by portfolio managers. From a top-down perspective, ESG aggregate portfolio metrics are available for the Fund manager to review through BlackRock&#x27;s Aladdin system. The Fund manager also considers environmental, social and governance criteria during post-investment monitoring and conducts regular portfolio risk reviews between the investment team and BlackRock’s Risk and Quantitative Analysis group. These reviews include the analysis and discussion of portfolio exposure to material ESG risks, where appropriate.&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-89&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Fund manager includes ESG considerations in combination with other information in the research phase of the investment process. This may include relevant third-party insights, as well as internal engagement commentary and input from BlackRock Investment Stewardship on governance issues. The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion, where appropriate, of the portfolio&#x27;s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate-related metrics, and other factors.&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-9&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Fund manager includes ESG considerations in the initial screening, sourcing and due diligence phases of the investment process. This may include the use of internal ESG due diligence templates to identify, analyze and document key ESG risks. Specialist consultants may also be appointed to support due diligence. Where appropriate, identified ESG risks are highlighted in Investment Committee materials and discussed at relevant Investment Committee meetings. This information may broadly inform investment decisions: ESG criteria are considered in combination with other information and often with a focus on evaluating asset liquidity and product market fit. The Fund manager also considers environmental, social and governance criteria during post-investment monitoring and conducts regular portfolio risk reviews between the investment team and BlackRock’s Risk and Quantitative Analysis group. These reviews include the analysis and discussion of portfolio exposure to material ESG risks, where appropriate.&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-90&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Fund manager includes ESG considerations in combination with other information in the research phase of the investment process. This may include relevant third-party insights, as well as internal engagement commentary and input from BlackRock Investment Stewardship on governance issues. The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion, where appropriate, of the portfolio&#x27;s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate-related metrics, and other factors.&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-91&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Fund manager includes ESG considerations in combination with other information in the research phase of the investment process. This may include relevant third-party insights, as well as internal engagement commentary and input from BlackRock Investment Stewardship on governance issues. The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion, where appropriate, of the portfolio&#x27;s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate-related metrics, and other factors.&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-92&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Fund manager includes ESG considerations in the investment research, portfolio construction, and investment monitoring phases of the investment process. The Fund manager maintains internal ESG scorecards for certain issuers under consideration for investment and certain existing issuers of publicly traded securities. These scorecards analyze and track internal and external research views across a range of environmental, social, and governance factors sourced from primary and third-party ESG information and research. Portfolio management teams may consider the sector and issuer ESG views and scores during portfolio construction. The Fund manager also considers ESG criteria during post-investment monitoring and conducts regular portfolio risk reviews between the investment team and BlackRock’s Risk and Quantitative Analysis group. These reviews include discussion of the portfolio&#x27;s exposure to material ESG risks, where appropriate.&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-93&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Fund manager includes ESG considerations in combination with other information in the research phase of the investment process. This may include relevant third-party insights, as well as internal engagement commentary and input from BlackRock Investment Stewardship on governance issues. The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion, where appropriate, of the portfolio&#x27;s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate-related metrics, and other factors.&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-94&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Fund manager includes ESG considerations in combination with other information in the research phase of the investment process. This may include relevant third-party insights, as well as internal engagement commentary and input from BlackRock Investment Stewardship on governance issues. The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion, where appropriate, of the portfolio&#x27;s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate-related metrics, and other factors.&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-95&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Fund manager includes ESG considerations in combination with other information in the research phase of the investment process. This may include relevant third-party insights, as well as internal engagement commentary and input from BlackRock Investment Stewardship on governance issues. The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group and with the Chief Investment Officers. These reviews include discussion, where appropriate, of the portfolio&#x27;s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate-related metrics, and other factors.&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-96&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Fund manager includes ESG considerations in combination with other information in the research and due diligence phase of the investment process. ESG information may be sourced internally or from third-party providers. The Fund manager&#x27;s ongoing monitoring of the portfolio involves regular portfolio risk reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group. These reviews include discussion, where appropriate, of the portfolio&#x27;s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate-related metrics, and other factors.&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-97&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Fund manager includes ESG considerations in combination with other information in the research and due diligence stage of the investment process. The Fund manager has developed internal research signals to help evaluate corporate issuers on climate, governance and human capital issues. ESG information may be sourced from both internal and external sources. The Fund manager conducts regular portfolio risk reviews with the Risk and Quantitative Analysis group. These reviews include discussion, where appropriate, of the portfolio&#x27;s exposure to material ESG risks, as well as exposure to sustainability-related business involvements, climate-related metrics, and other factors.&quot;}],&quot;esg-stmt-global&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;BlackRock considers many investment risks in our processes. In order to seek the best risk-adjusted returns for our clients, we manage material risks and opportunities that could impact portfolios, including financially material Environmental, Social and/or Governance (ESG) data or information, where available. See our &lt;a href=\&quot;https://www.blackrock.com/corporate/literature/publication/blk-esg-investment-statement-web.pdf\&quot;&gt;Firm Wide ESG Integration Statement&lt;/a&gt; for more information on this approach and fund documentation for how these material risks are considered within this product, where applicable.&quot;}],&quot;exposure-breakdowns.disclaimer&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Allocations are subject to change.&quot;}],&quot;exposure-breakdowns.geography.disclaimer&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Geographic exposure relates principally to the domicile of the issuers of the securities held in the product, added together and then expressed as a percentage of the product’s total holdings. However, in some instances it can reflect the location where the issuer of the securities carries out much of their business.&quot;}],&quot;fee-table.secondary.sub-title&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;On Managed Assets&quot;}],&quot;fee-table.sub-title&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;as of current prospectus&quot;}],&quot;fund-header.disclaimer&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=\&quot;emphasis\&quot;&gt;Important Information: Capital at Risk.&lt;/span&gt; The value of investments and the income from them can fall as well as rise and are not guaranteed. Investors may not get back the amount originally invested.&lt;/p&gt;&quot;},{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The value of equities and equity-related securities can be affected by daily stock market movements. Other influential factors include political, economic news, company earnings and significant corporate events. The benchmark index only excludes companies engaging in certain activities inconsistent with ESG criteria if such activities exceed the thresholds determined by the index provider.  Such ESG screening may reduce the potential investment universe and this may adversely affect the value of the Fund’s investments compared to a fund without such screening. Emerging markets are generally more sensitive to economic and political conditions than developed markets. Other factors include greater &#x27;Liquidity Risk&#x27;, restrictions on investment or transfer of assets, failed/delayed delivery of securities or payments to the Fund and sustainability-related risks. Currency Risk: The Fund invests in other currencies. Changes in exchange rates will therefore affect the value of the investment.&quot;},{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;All currency hedged share classes of this fund use derivatives to hedge currency risk. The use of derivatives for a share class could pose a potential risk of contagion (also known as spill-over) to other share classes in the fund. The fund’s management company will ensure appropriate procedures are in place to minimise contagion risk to other share class. Using the drop down box directly below the name of the fund, you can view a list of all share classes in the fund – currency hedged share classes are indicated by the word “Hedged” in the name of the share class. In addition, a full list of all currency hedged share classes is available on request from the fund’s management company&quot;}],&quot;fund-header.documents&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;{type=GLS;material=SFDR Web Disclosure}{type=GLS;material=UKPRIIP}{type=GLS;material=KIID~Simplified Prospectus}{type=GLS;material=Fact Sheet}{type=GLS;material=Prospectus}{type=GLS;material=CFD}&quot;}],&quot;fund-of-fund.disclaimer&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;If the Fund invests in any underlying fund, certain portfolio information, including sustainability characteristics and business-involvement metrics, provided for the Fund may include information (on a look-through basis) of such underlying fund, to the extent available.&quot;}],&quot;fund_objective&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The fund aims to achieve a return on your investment, through a combination of capital growth and income on the Funds’ assets, which reflects the return of the MSCI ACWI Screened Index, the Fund’s benchmark index (Index).&quot;}],&quot;fund_overview.fund_overview&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Performance is not shown as the Fund has a performance history of less than 1 year. You should read the Prospectus and the Key Investor Information Document (KIID) for each fund in which you want to invest.&quot;}],&quot;fund_overview.less_than_year&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Performance is not shown as the Fund has a performance history of less than 1 year. You should read the Prospectus and the Key Investor Information Document (KIID) for each fund in which you want to invest.&quot;}],&quot;fund_talking_points&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Invests in a sub-set of equity securities which are part of the MSCI ACWI Index (the “Parent Index”) by excluding companies from the Parent Index based on the index provider’s exclusionary criteria.&quot;},{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Screens exposure to controversial and nuclear weapons, producers of tobacco or civilian firearms, United Nations Global Compact violators, and companies involved in very severe controversies. Companies are also excluded if the revenue they generate from any of the following activities exceeds the threshold defined in the index methodology: thermal coal mining; unconventional oil and gas extraction; thermal coal-based power generation; arctic oil and gas extraction; the distribution, retail, supply, or licensing of tobacco-related products; the distribution of civilian firearms; or the production or distribution of palm oil.&quot;},{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Designed for investors looking to target a reduction of greenhouse gas emission intensity as defined in the index methodology, while maintaining a risk profile similar to traditional benchmarks&quot;}],&quot;glossary&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;&lt;strong&gt;Total Expense Ratio (TER):&lt;/strong&gt; A measure of the total costs associated with managing and operating a fund. The TER consists primarily of the management fee plus other expenses such as trustee, custody, or operating expenses. It is expressed as a percentage of the fund&#x27;s total net asset value.&quot;},{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;&lt;strong&gt;Distribution yield:&lt;/strong&gt; The distribution yield represents the ratio of distributed income over the last 12 months to the fund&#x27;s current Net Asset Value.&quot;},{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;&lt;strong&gt;Product Structure:&lt;/strong&gt; Indicates whether the fund buys the actual underlying securities in the index (i.e. Physical) or whether the fund gains exposure to those securities by buying derivatives, such as swaps (known as ’Synthetic’). Swaps are a form of contract that promises to provide the return of the security to the fund, but the fund does not hold the actual security. This can introduce a risk that the counterparty defaults on the “promise” or contract.&quot;},{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;&lt;strong&gt;Methodology:&lt;/strong&gt; Indicates whether the product is holding all index securities in the same weight as the index (replicating) or whether an optimised subset of index securities is used (optimised/sampled) in order to efficiently track index performance.&quot;}],&quot;glossary.dailyliquidity&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;&lt;strong&gt;Daily Maturing Asset: &lt;/strong&gt;Are presented as a percentage of the fund’s total assets on the date stated&quot;}],&quot;glossary.weeklyliquidity&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;&lt;strong&gt;Weekly Maturing Asset:&lt;/strong&gt; The average of the weekly determinations of the difference between the total assets of the Fund attributable to an Allocated Sleeve and the total liabilities of the Fund attributable to such Allocated Sleeve, determined at the close of the last business day of each week.&quot;}],&quot;holdings.disclaimer&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Detailed Holdings and Analytics contains detailed portfolio holdings information and select analytics.&quot;}],&quot;holdings.sec-lending.content&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;&lt;p&gt;Securities lending is an established and well regulated activity in the investment management industry. It involves the transfer of securities (such as shares or bonds) from a Lender (in this case, the iShares fund) to a third-party (the Borrower). The Borrower will give the Lender collateral (the Borrower’s pledge) in the form of shares, bonds or cash, and will also pay the Lender a fee. This fee provides additional income for the fund and thus can help to reduce the total cost of ownership of an ETF.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;At BlackRock, securities lending is a core investment management function with dedicated trading, research and technology capabilities. The lending programme is designed to deliver superior absolute returns to clients, whilst maintaining a low risk profile. Funds participating in securities lending retain 62.5% of the income, while BlackRock receives 37.5% of the income and covers all the operational costs resulting from securities lending transactions.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&quot;}],&quot;holdings.sec-lending.content-table&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;&lt;div class=\&quot;collateral-matrix\&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;p class=\&quot;main-disclaimer oneds-body-m no-top-margin\&quot;&gt;\n        The below table shows the Loan/Collateral Combinations and Collateral\n        Levels for our European Lending funds.\n      &lt;/p&gt;\n\n      &lt;div class=\&quot;table-wrapper\&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;table class=\&quot;collateral-table oneds-body-m-compact\&quot;&gt;\n          &lt;colgroup&gt;\n            &lt;col /&gt;\n            &lt;col /&gt;\n            &lt;col /&gt;\n            &lt;col /&gt;\n            &lt;col /&gt;\n          &lt;/colgroup&gt;\n          &lt;thead&gt;\n            &lt;tr class=\&quot;table-title-row\&quot;&gt;\n              &lt;th&gt;&lt;/th&gt;\n              &lt;th&gt;&lt;/th&gt;\n              &lt;th class=\&quot;table-title oneds-body-s-compact-bold\&quot; colspan=\&quot;3\&quot;&gt;\n                COLLATERAL TYPES\n              &lt;/th&gt;\n            &lt;/tr&gt;\n            &lt;tr class=\&quot;columns oneds-body-s-compact\&quot;&gt;\n              &lt;th&gt;&lt;/th&gt;\n              &lt;th&gt;&lt;/th&gt;\n              &lt;th&gt;Equities&lt;/th&gt;\n              &lt;th&gt;Government, Supranational and Agency Bonds&lt;/th&gt;\n              &lt;th&gt;Cash (Not for Reinvestment)&lt;/th&gt;\n            &lt;/tr&gt;\n          &lt;/thead&gt;\n          &lt;tbody&gt;\n            &lt;tr&gt;\n              &lt;td class=\&quot;loan-types-col oneds-body-s-compact-bold\&quot; rowspan=\&quot;3\&quot;&gt;\n                LOAN TYPES\n              &lt;/td&gt;\n              &lt;td class=\&quot;row-title oneds-body-s-compact\&quot;&gt;Equities&lt;/td&gt;\n              &lt;td class=\&quot;value-cell\&quot;&gt;105% - 112%&lt;/td&gt;\n              &lt;td class=\&quot;value-cell\&quot;&gt;105% - 106%&lt;/td&gt;\n              &lt;td class=\&quot;value-cell\&quot;&gt;105% - 108%&lt;/td&gt;\n            &lt;/tr&gt;\n            &lt;tr&gt;\n              &lt;td class=\&quot;row-title oneds-body-s-compact\&quot;&gt;Government Bonds&lt;/td&gt;\n              &lt;td class=\&quot;value-cell\&quot;&gt;110% - 112%&lt;/td&gt;\n              &lt;td class=\&quot;value-cell\&quot;&gt;102.5% - 106%&lt;/td&gt;\n              &lt;td class=\&quot;value-cell\&quot;&gt;102.5% - 105%&lt;/td&gt;\n            &lt;/tr&gt;\n            &lt;tr&gt;\n              &lt;td class=\&quot;row-title oneds-body-s-compact\&quot;&gt;Corporate Bonds&lt;/td&gt;\n              &lt;td class=\&quot;value-cell\&quot;&gt;110% - 112%&lt;/td&gt;\n              &lt;td class=\&quot;value-cell\&quot;&gt;104% - 106%&lt;/td&gt;\n              &lt;td class=\&quot;value-cell\&quot;&gt;103.5% - 105%&lt;/td&gt;\n            &lt;/tr&gt;\n          &lt;/tbody&gt;\n        &lt;/table&gt;\n      &lt;/div&gt;\n\n      &lt;div class=\&quot;main-disclaimer oneds-body-m\&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;p&gt;\n          We also accept selected physically replicating Equity, Government\n          Bond, Credit and Commodity ETFs as collateral.\n        &lt;/p&gt;\n        &lt;p&gt;\n          Collateral parameters depend on the collateral and the loan\n          combination, and the over collateralisation level may range from\n          102.5% to 112%. In this context, “Over Collateralisation” means that\n          the aggregate market value of collateral taken will exceed the overall\n          on-loan value. Collateral parameters are reviewed on an ongoing bases\n          and are subject to change.\n        &lt;/p&gt;\n        &lt;p&gt;\n          With securities lending there is a risk of loss should the borrower\n          default before the securities are returned, and due to market\n          movements, the value of collateral held has fallen and/or the value of\n          the securities on loan has risen.\n        &lt;/p&gt;\n      &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n\n    &lt;style&gt;\n      /* Container + table base */\n      .collateral-matrix table.collateral-table {\n        border-collapse: collapse;\n        width: 100%;\n        margin: var(--oneds-space-fluid-m, 32px) auto;\n      }\n\n      /* Base cell styles */\n      .collateral-matrix table.collateral-table th,\n      .collateral-matrix table.collateral-table td {\n        padding: var(--oneds-space-fluid-xs, 16px);\n        text-align: center;\n      }\n\n      /* Column widths */\n      .collateral-matrix table.collateral-table colgroup col:nth-child(1),\n      .collateral-matrix table.collateral-table colgroup col:nth-child(2) {\n        width: 75px;\n      }\n\n      .collateral-matrix table.collateral-table colgroup col:nth-child(3) {\n        width: 220px;\n      }\n\n      .collateral-matrix table.collateral-table colgroup col:nth-child(4) {\n        width: 260px;\n      }\n\n      .collateral-matrix table.collateral-table colgroup col:nth-child(5) {\n        width: 220px;\n      }\n\n      /* Row/column specific cells */\n      .collateral-matrix table.collateral-table td.loan-types-col {\n        border-right: 1px solid #ccc;\n        vertical-align: middle;\n        text-align: center;\n        padding-left: 0;\n      }\n\n      .collateral-matrix table.collateral-table td.row-title {\n        text-align: right;\n      }\n\n      .collateral-matrix table.collateral-table td.value-cell {\n        border: 1px solid #ccc;\n      }\n\n      /* First row top border; left thick border after row-title */\n      .collateral-matrix\n        table.collateral-table\n        tbody\n        tr:first-child\n        td.value-cell {\n        border-top: 4px solid #000;\n      }\n\n      .collateral-matrix\n        table.collateral-table\n        tbody\n        tr\n        td.row-title\n        + td.value-cell {\n        border-left: 4px solid #000;\n      }\n\n      /* Mobile adjustments */\n      @media (max-width: 768px) {\n        .collateral-matrix table.collateral-table td.loan-types-col {\n          writing-mode: vertical-lr;\n          text-orientation: mixed;\n          white-space: nowrap;\n          transform: rotate(180deg);\n          transform-origin: center;\n          padding-left: 12px;\n          padding-right: 0;\n        }\n\n        .collateral-matrix table.collateral-table th,\n        .collateral-matrix table.collateral-table td {\n          padding: var(--oneds-space-fluid-xs, 16px);\n        }\n\n        .collateral-matrix table.collateral-table td.value-cell {\n          padding: 8px;\n          min-width: 132px;\n          min-height: 44px;\n          white-space: nowrap;\n          vertical-align: middle;\n        }\n      }\n\n      /* Title underline */\n      .collateral-matrix .table-title {\n        border-bottom: 1px solid #ccc;\n      }\n\n      /* Column header styling */\n      .collateral-matrix .columns th {\n        font-weight: normal;\n        vertical-align: bottom;\n      }\n\n      /* Disclaimer */\n      .collateral-matrix .main-disclaimer p {\n        margin-bottom: var(--oneds-space-fluid-s, 24px);\n      }\n\n      .collateral-matrix .main-disclaimer.no-top-margin {\n        margin-top: 0;\n      }\n\n      .collateral-matrix\n        .main-disclaimer[data-disclaimer-fragment=\&quot;holdings.sec-lending.content-table\&quot;] {\n        margin-top: 0;\n        max-width: 100%;\n      }\n\n      .collateral-matrix .table-wrapper {\n        overflow-x: auto;\n        width: 100%;\n      }\n    &lt;/style&gt;&quot;}],&quot;holdings.sec-lending.disclaimer&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Collateral Holdings shown on this page are provided on days where the fund participating in securities lending had an open loan.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;The information in the Collateral Holdings table relates to securities obtained in the collateral basket under the securities lending programme for the fund in question. The information contained in this material is derived from proprietary and non-proprietary sources deemed by BlackRock to be reliable, is not necessarily all inclusive and is not guaranteed as to accuracy. Reliance upon information in this material is at the sole discretion of the reader. The primary risk in securities lending is that a borrower will default on their commitment to return lent securities while the value of the liquidated collateral does not exceed the cost of repurchasing the securities and the fund suffers a loss in respect of the short-fall.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&quot;}],&quot;important.information&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=\&quot;emphasis\&quot;&gt;Important Information: Capital at Risk.&lt;/span&gt; The value of investments and the income from them can fall as well as rise and are not guaranteed. Investors may not get back the amount originally invested.&lt;/p&gt;&quot;}],&quot;index_overview.index_overview&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Index Overview&quot;}],&quot;kiid-exchange-traded-fund.header&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;fred.investorClassCode USD fred.useOfProfit&quot;}],&quot;kiid-fund-isin.label&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;ISIN :&quot;}],&quot;kiid-fund-objective-end-disclaimer.text&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The shares are listed on one or more stock exchanges and may be traded in currencies other than their base currency. The performance of your shares may be affected by this currency difference. In normal circumstances, only authorised participants (e.g. select financial institutions) may deal in shares (or interests in shares) directly with the Fund. Other investors can deal in shares (or interests in shares) daily through an intermediary on stock exchange (s) on which the shares are traded. Indicative net asset value is published on relevant stock exchanges websites.&quot;}],&quot;kiid-fund-objective.distributing&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Your shares will be accumulating shares (i.e. income will be included in their value).&quot;}],&quot;kiid-fund-objective.text&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Share Class is a share class of a Fund which aims to achieve a return on your investment, through a combination of capital growth and income on the Funds’ assets, which reflects the return of the MSCI ACWI Screened Index, the Fund’s benchmark index (Index).&quot;},{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Share Class is a share class of a Fund which aims to achieve a return on your investment, through a combination of capital growth and income on the Fund’s assets, which reflects the return of the MSCI ACWI Screened Index, the Fund’s benchmark index (Index).&quot;},{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Share Class, via the Fund, is passively managed, and aims to invest in equity securities (e.g. shares) that, so far as possible and practicable, make up the Index.&quot;},{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Index measures the performance of a sub-set of equity securities which are part of the MSCI ACWI Index (the “Parent Index”) which excludes companies from the Parent Index based on the index provider’s environmental, social and governance (ESG) exclusionary criteria. The Parent Index measures the performance of large and mid-capitalisation companies across developed and emerging markets which comply with MSCI&#x27;s size, liquidity and free-float criteria.&quot;},{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Index excludes companies which are involved in certain business lines/activities, as set out in the Fund’s prospectus, including: controversial weapons, nuclear weapons, tobacco, civilian firearms, thermal coal-based power generation, fossil fuel extraction, palm oil or arctic oil and gas. Companies that are classified as violating UN Global Compact principles are also excluded from the Index. The Index also excludes companies which do not meet the minimum MSCI ESG Controversy Scores to be eligible. Companies may, where necessary, be further excluded in order for the Index to reach the level of the reduction of carbon emission intensity relative to the Parent Index set by the index provider.&quot;},{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Investment Manager will take into account the above ESG criteria only when selecting the securities to be held directly by the Fund. The Fund may also obtain indirect exposure to securities considered not to satisfy these ESG criteria. The Index is free-float adjusted market capitalisation weighted and rebalances on a quarterly basis.&quot;},{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Fund adopts a binding and significant ESG integration approach to sustainable investing. This means that the Fund will integrate ESG information into its investment process to optimise exposure to issuers to achieve a higher ESG rating compared to the Parent Index.&quot;},{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The Fund uses optimising techniques to achieve a similar return to its Index. The Fund may use financial derivative instruments for direct investment purposes. The Fund may also engage in short term secured lending of its investments to certain eligible third parties to generate additional income to offset the costs of the Fund.&quot;}],&quot;kiid-performance-historic-performance.text&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Historic performance to 31 December 2025&quot;}],&quot;kiid-practical-info.text&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The indicative intra-day net asset value of the Share Class is published on relevant stock exchanges websites.&quot;}],&quot;kiid-risk-non-srri&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Counterparty Risk: The insolvency of any institutions providing services such as safekeeping of assets or acting as counterparty to derivatives or other instruments, may expose the Share Class to financial loss.&quot;}],&quot;kiid-risk-non-srri-main.text-new&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Particular risks not adequately captured by the risk indicator include:&quot;}],&quot;kiid-risk-non-srri-new&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Counterparty Risk: The insolvency of any institutions providing services such as safekeeping of assets or acting as counterparty to derivatives or other instruments, may expose the Share Class to financial loss.&quot;},{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Liquidity Risk: Lower liquidity means there are insufficient buyers or sellers to allow the Fund to sell or buy investments readily.&quot;}],&quot;kiid-risk-srri&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Emerging markets are generally more sensitive to economic and political conditions than developed markets. Other factors include greater &#x27;Liquidity Risk&#x27;, restrictions on investment or transfer of assets, failed/delayed delivery of securities or payments to the Fund and sustainability-related risks.&quot;},{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Currency Risk: The Fund invests in other currencies. Changes in exchange rates will therefore affect the value of the investment.&quot;},{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The value of equities and equity-related securities can be affected by daily stock market movements. Other influential factors include political, economic news, company earnings and significant corporate events.&quot;},{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;The benchmark index only excludes companies engaging in certain activities inconsistent with ESG criteria if such activities exceed the thresholds determined by the index provider.  Such ESG screening may reduce the potential investment universe and this may adversely affect the value of the Fund’s investments compared to a fund without such screening.&quot;}],&quot;kiid-share-class-name.header&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;fred.investorClassCode USD fred.useOfProfit&quot;}],&quot;label.10k_growth_chart.beginning_value&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Beginning Value&quot;}],&quot;label.10k_growth_chart.date&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Date&quot;}],&quot;label.10k_growth_chart.ending_value&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Ending Value&quot;}],&quot;label.10kgrowthchart.growth&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Growth&quot;}],&quot;label.achieved-tracking-error&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Achieved Tracking-&lt;br /&gt;Error % (3 Year)&quot;}],&quot;label.as_of&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;as at&quot;}],&quot;label.calendar_year&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Calendar Year&quot;}],&quot;label.country_breakdown.other_includes&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Other Includes&quot;}],&quot;label.dealinginformation.dealingdeadline&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Trading Deadline&quot;}],&quot;label.documentdate&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;All other data as at&quot;}],&quot;label.exchange.bloombergcode&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Bloomberg Ticker&quot;}],&quot;label.exchange.exchangename&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Exchange&quot;}],&quot;label.exchange.other_exchange&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;This product is also listed on:&quot;}],&quot;label.exchange.reuterscode&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;RIC&quot;}],&quot;label.exchange.sedol&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;SEDOL&quot;}],&quot;label.exchange.ticker&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Ticker&quot;}],&quot;label.exchange.tradingcurrency&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Trading Currency&quot;}],&quot;label.exchange.valoren&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Valor&quot;}],&quot;label.exchange.wkn&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;WKN&quot;}],&quot;label.factsheet&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Factsheet&quot;}],&quot;label.feedata.annualmgtcharges&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Annual Management Fee*&quot;}],&quot;label.feedata.forwardfee&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Forward Structure Costs&quot;}],&quot;label.feedata.forwardfee.to&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;to&quot;}],&quot;label.feedata.managementexpenseratiomer&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Management Expense Ratio (MER)&quot;}],&quot;label.feedata.managementfee&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Management Fee&quot;}],&quot;label.feedata.managementfeeincludesservicefee&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Management Fee&quot;}],&quot;label.feedata.managementfeeupto&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Management Fee (up to)&quot;}],&quot;label.feedata.maximumannualotherexpenses&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Maximum Annual Other Expenses&quot;}],&quot;label.feedata.merbeforewaiversandabsorptions&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;MER Before Waivers and Absorptions&quot;}],&quot;label.feedata.ongoingchargesestimatedflag&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;&lt;b&gt;Estimated Ongoing Charge&lt;/b&gt;&quot;}],&quot;label.feedata.servicefeeincludedinmer&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Service Fee&quot;}],&quot;label.feedata.totalannualfee&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Total Annual Fee&quot;}],&quot;label.feedata.totalexpenseratio&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Total Expense Ratio&quot;}],&quot;label.firmdata.subadvisor&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Investment Sub-Advisor&quot;}],&quot;label.fund.overview&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;FUND OVERVIEW&quot;}],&quot;label.fundDetails.trackingerror&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;3 Year Tracking Error&quot;}],&quot;label.fund_characteristics.avg_yield_to_maturity&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Weighted Average Yield To Maturity&quot;}],&quot;label.fund_characteristics.duration&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Duration&quot;}],&quot;label.fund_characteristics.effectiveduration&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Effective Duration&quot;}],&quot;label.fund_characteristics.market_capitalisation&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Market Capitalisation (millions)&quot;}],&quot;label.fund_characteristics.nominalwal&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Nominal Weighted Average Life (WAL)&quot;}],&quot;label.fund_characteristics.portfolio_yield&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Portfolio Yield&quot;}],&quot;label.fund_characteristics.sharperatio&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Sharpe Ratio&quot;}],&quot;label.fund_characteristics.standarddeviationbeta&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Standard Deviation&quot;}],&quot;label.fund_characteristics.term_to_maturity.yrs&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;yrs&quot;}],&quot;label.fund_characteristics.weightedavgcoupon&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Weighted Average Coupon&quot;}],&quot;label.fund_characteristics.weightedavgmaturity&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Weighted Average Maturity&quot;}],&quot;label.fund_characteristics.yield_to_worst&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Yield to Worst&quot;}],&quot;label.fund_details.eligible_for_registered_plans&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Eligible for Registered Plans&quot;}],&quot;label.fund_specific_risk_p1_continued&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;&lt;b&gt;(Continued on page 2)&lt;/b&gt;&quot;}],&quot;label.fund_specific_risk_p2_continued&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;&lt;strong&gt;Key Risks Continued: &lt;/strong&gt;&quot;}],&quot;label.fundamentaldata.pricetobook&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Price to Book Ratio&quot;}],&quot;label.fundamentaldata.pricetoearnings&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Price to Earnings (TTM) Ratio&quot;}],&quot;label.fundamentaldata.standarddeviation3yr&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Standard Deviation (3yrs)&quot;}],&quot;label.fundamentaldata.termtomaturity&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Term to Maturity&quot;}],&quot;label.fundcharacteristics.effectiveduration&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Effective Duration&quot;}],&quot;label.fundcharacteristics.weightedaverageytm&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Weighted Avg YTM&quot;}],&quot;label.fundnavdata.totalnetassets&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Net Assets of Fund&quot;}],&quot;label.header.performance_holding_date&quot;:[{&quot;metadata&quot;:null,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Per