t;5,220.53&quot;,&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Benchmark Level&quot;,&quot;asOfLabel&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;infoBubble&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;prefix&quot;:&quot;USD &quot;,&quot;value&quot;:5220.532199,&quot;returnType&quot;:false,&quot;associatedReturnType&quot;:false,&quot;fullName&quot;:&quot;fundamentalsAndRisk.levelAmount&quot;},&quot;numHoldings&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;numHoldings&quot;,&quot;visible&quot;:true,&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;asOf&quot;:true,&quot;hideNullData&quot;:false,&quot;mobileEnabled&quot;:true,&quot;sortOrder&quot;:3,&quot;asOfDate&quot;:20260922,&quot;formattedAsOfDate&quot;:&quot;22/Sept/2026&quot;,&quot;formattedValue&quot;:&quot;1795&quot;,&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Number of Holdings&quot;,&quot;asOfLabel&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;infoBubble&quot;:&quot;The number of holdings in the fund excluding cash positions and derivatives exposures. Derivatives are contracts used by the fund to gain exposure to an investment without buying it directly.  They can be used in a number of ways. For example a &amp;#39;currency forward&amp;#39; derivative contract can be used to &amp;#39;hedge&amp;#39; or aim to mitigate the effects of changes in exchange rates.&quot;,&quot;prefix&quot;:null,&quot;value&quot;:1795,&quot;returnType&quot;:false,&quot;associatedReturnType&quot;:false,&quot;fullName&quot;:&quot;fundamentalsAndRisk.numHoldings&quot;},&quot;priceBook&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;priceBook&quot;,&quot;visible&quot;:true,&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;asOf&quot;:true,&quot;hideNullData&quot;:false,&quot;mobileEnabled&quot;:true,&quot;sortOrder&quot;:36,&quot;asOfDate&quot;:20260922,&quot;formattedAsOfDate&quot;:&quot;22/Sept/2026&quot;,&quot;formattedValue&quot;:&quot;4.06&quot;,&quot;label&quot;:&quot;P/B Ratio&quot;,&quot;asOfLabel&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;infoBubble&quot;:&quot;The price to book (P/B) value ratio is a fundamental measure used to determine if an investment is valued appropriately. The book value of a company is a measure of how much a company&amp;#39;s assets are worth assuming the company&amp;#39;s debts are paid off. Negative book values are excluded from this calculation and holding price to book ratios over 25 are set to 25.&quot;,&quot;prefix&quot;:null,&quot;value&quot;:4.05681,&quot;returnType&quot;:false,&quot;associatedReturnType&quot;:false,&quot;fullName&quot;:&quot;fundamentalsAndRisk.priceBook&quot;},&quot;priceEarnings&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;priceEarnings&quot;,&quot;visible&quot;:true,&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;asOf&quot;:true,&quot;hideNullData&quot;:false,&quot;mobileEnabled&quot;:true,&quot;sortOrder&quot;:35,&quot;asOfDate&quot;:20260922,&quot;formattedAsOfDate&quot;:&quot;22/Sept/2026&quot;,&quot;formattedValue&quot;:&quot;25.85&quot;,&quot;label&quot;:&quot;P/E Ratio&quot;,&quot;asOfLabel&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;infoBubble&quot;:&quot;The price to earnings ratio (P/E) is a fundamental measure used to determine if an investment is valued appropriately. Each holdings&amp;#39; P/E is the latest closing price divided by the latest 12 months&amp;#39; earnings per share. Negative earnings are excluded, extraordinary items are excluded, and P/E ratios over 60 are set to 60.&quot;,&quot;prefix&quot;:null,&quot;value&quot;:25.85255,&quot;returnType&quot;:false,&quot;associatedReturnType&quot;:false,&quot;fullName&quot;:&quot;fundamentalsAndRisk.priceEarnings&quot;},&quot;rocPct&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;rocPct&quot;,&quot;visible&quot;:false,&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;asOf&quot;:false,&quot;hideNullData&quot;:false,&quot;mobileEnabled&quot;:false,&quot;sortOrder&quot;:null,&quot;asOfDate&quot;:null,&quot;formattedAsOfDate&quot;:null,&quot;formattedValue&quot;:&quot;-&quot;,&quot;label&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;asOfLabel&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;infoBubble&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;prefix&quot;:null,&quot;value&quot;:null,&quot;returnType&quot;:false,&quot;associatedReturnType&quot;:false,&quot;fullName&quot;:&quot;fundamentalsAndRisk.rocPct&quot;},&quot;rocPct12Month&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;rocPct12Month&quot;,&quot;visible&quot;:false,&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;asOf&quot;:false,&quot;hideNullData&quot;:false,&quot;mobileEnabled&quot;:false,&quot;sortOrder&quot;:null,&quot;asOfDate&quot;:null,&quot;formattedAsOfDate&quot;:null,&quot;formattedValue&quot;:&quot;-&quot;,&quot;label&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;asOfLabel&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;infoBubble&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;prefix&quot;:null,&quot;value&quot;:null,&quot;returnType&quot;:false,&quot;associatedReturnType&quot;:false,&quot;fullName&quot;:&quot;fundamentalsAndRisk.rocPct12Month&quot;},&quot;threeYrBetaFund&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;threeYrBetaFund&quot;,&quot;visible&quot;:true,&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;asOf&quot;:true,&quot;hideNullData&quot;:false,&quot;mobileEnabled&quot;:true,&quot;sortOrder&quot;:33,&quot;asOfDate&quot;:null,&quot;formattedAsOfDate&quot;:&quot;-&quot;,&quot;formattedValue&quot;:&quot;-&quot;,&quot;label&quot;:&quot;3y Beta&quot;,&quot;asOfLabel&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;infoBubble&quot;:&quot;Beta is a measure of the tendency of securities to move with the market as a whole. A beta of 1 indicates that the security&amp;#39;s price will move with the market. A beta less than 1 indicates the security tends to be less volatile than the market, while a beta greater than 1 indicates the security is more volatile than the market.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Calculated vs. Benchmark Index&quot;,&quot;prefix&quot;:null,&quot;value&quot;:null,&quot;returnType&quot;:false,&quot;associatedReturnType&quot;:false,&quot;fullName&quot;:&quot;fundamentalsAndRisk.threeYrBetaFund&quot;},&quot;volatilitySourced3YrAnnualized&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;volatilitySourced3YrAnnualized&quot;,&quot;visible&quot;:true,&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;asOf&quot;:true,&quot;hideNullData&quot;:false,&quot;mobileEnabled&quot;:true,&quot;sortOrder&quot;:32,&quot;asOfDate&quot;:null,&quot;formattedAsOfDate&quot;:null,&quot;formattedValue&quot;:&quot;-&quot;,&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Standard Deviation (3y)&quot;,&quot;asOfLabel&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;infoBubble&quot;:&quot;Standard deviation measures how dispersed returns are around the average. A higher standard deviation indicates that returns are spread out over a larger range of values and thus, more volatile.&quot;,&quot;prefix&quot;:null,&quot;value&quot;:null,&quot;returnType&quot;:false,&quot;associatedReturnType&quot;:false,&quot;fullName&quot;:&quot;fundamentalsAndRisk.volatilitySourced3YrAnnualized&quot;}},&quot;hasData&quot;:true,&quot;subContainersByNameMap&quot;:{},&quot;default&quot;:true,&quot;granted&quot;:true}},&quot;sortOrder&quot;:null,&quot;componentConfig&quot;:{&quot;complianceRules&quot;:[{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;[fundamentalsAndRisk] 12. EMEA, APAC, LATAM | ALL | COND: The product is less than three years old. | EFF: Nullify three- and five-year volatility benchmark and beta metrics | AE, AT, BE, BG, BR, CH, CL, CN, CO, CY, CZ, DE, DK, EE, ES, FI, FR, GB, GG, GI, GR, HK, HR, HU, IE, IL, IM, IS, IT, JE, LI, LT, LV, MT, MX, NL, NO, PL, PT, RO, SA, SE, SG, SI, SK, TW, ZA&quot;,&quot;expression&quot;:&quot;(#product?.inceptionDate &gt; #threeYearsCutOffDate)&quot;,&quot;actions&quot;:[{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;NULLIFY_VALUE_DASH_FORMATTED&quot;,&quot;containerPath&quot;:&quot;default&quot;,&quot;items&quot;:[&quot;threeYrVolatilityBenchmarkAnnualized&quot;,&quot;fiveYrVolatilityBenchmarkAnnualized&quot;,&quot;threeYrBetaFund&quot;,&quot;fiveYrBetaFund&quot;,&quot;simpleAlphaThreeYear&quot;,&quot;simpleRsquaredThreeYear&quot;,&quot;simpleBetaThreeYear&quot;,&quot;threeYrVolatilityTarget&quot;,&quot;fiveYrVolatilityTarget&quot;,&quot;threeYrVolatilityTarget2&quot;,&quot;fiveYrVolatilityTarget2&quot;,&quot;threeYrVolatilityConstraint&quot;,&quot;fiveYrVolatilityConstraint&quot;,&quot;threeYrVolatilityConstraint2&quot;,&quot;fiveYrVolatilityConstraint2&quot;,&quot;threeYrVolatilityComparator&quot;,&quot;fiveYrVolatilityComparator&quot;,&quot;th