3"></div><div class="_scrollContainer_1a71w_7 _freeHeight_1a71w_14"><table class="facts-table"><tbody class="facts-table-body"><tr class="data-item oneds-body-m-compact col-numHoldings" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-row-numHoldings"><th class="caption" tabindex="-1"><div class="caption-wrapper"><span class="label" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-numHoldings-label" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-numHoldings-label">Number of Holdings</span><span class="info-bubble-container"><button id="infoBubble-ad047583-5d7b-454a-8eb4-15d3b6372930" class="product-info-bubble" aria-haspopup="true" aria-label="More Info: " aria-expanded="false" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-numHoldings-infoBubble" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-numHoldings-infoBubble" title="The number of holdings in the fund excluding cash positions and derivatives exposures. Derivatives are contracts used by the fund to gain exposure to an investment without buying it directly. They can be used in a number of ways. For example a &#x27;currency forward&#x27; derivative contract can be used to &#x27;hedge&#x27; or aim to mitigate the effects of changes in exchange rates."><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 18 16" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><g id="Circle-info"><path id="Vector" d="M8 16C10.1217 16 12.1566 15.1571 13.6569 13.6569C15.1571 12.1566 16 10.1217 16 8C16 5.87827 15.1571 3.84344 13.6569 2.34315C12.1566 0.842855 10.1217 0 8 0C5.87827 0 3.84344 0.842855 2.34314 2.34315C0.842853 3.84344 0 5.87827 0 8C0 10.1217 0.842853 12.1566 2.34314 13.6569C3.84344 15.1571 5.87827 16 8 16ZM6.75 10.5H7.5V8.5H6.75H6V7H6.75H8.25H9V7.75V10.5H9.25H10V12H9.25H6.75H6V10.5H6.75ZM9 6H7V4H9V6Z" fill="black"></path></g></svg></button></span></div><span><div class="as-of-date oneds-body-s-compact" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-numHoldings-asOf" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-numHoldings-asOf">as of 22/Sept/2026</div></span></th><td class="data oneds-body-l-bold" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-numHoldings" tabindex="-1" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-numHoldings-data">1795</td></tr><tr class="data-item oneds-body-m-compact col-benchmarkTicker" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-row-benchmarkTicker"><th class="caption" tabindex="-1"><div class="caption-wrapper"><span class="label" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-benchmarkTicker-label" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-benchmarkTicker-label">Benchmark Ticker</span></div><span></span></th><td class="data oneds-body-l-bold" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-benchmarkTicker" tabindex="-1" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-benchmarkTicker-data">NU722376</td></tr><tr class="data-item oneds-body-m-compact col-threeYrBetaFund" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-row-threeYrBetaFund"><th class="caption" tabindex="-1"><div class="caption-wrapper"><span class="label" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-threeYrBetaFund-label" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-threeYrBetaFund-label">3y Beta</span><span class="info-bubble-container"><button id="infoBubble-f8a025b0-29d1-4244-b513-24c05972d4e8" class="product-info-bubble" aria-haspopup="true" aria-label="More Info: " aria-expanded="false" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-threeYrBetaFund-infoBubble" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-threeYrBetaFund-infoBubble" title="Beta is a measure of the tendency of securities to move with the market as a whole. A beta of 1 indicates that the security&#x27;s price will move with the market. A beta less than 1 indicates the security tends to be less volatile than the market, while a beta greater than 1 indicates the security is more volatile than the market.Calculated vs. Benchmark Index"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 18 16" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><g id="Circle-info"><path id="Vector" d="M8 16C10.1217 16 12.1566 15.1571 13.6569 13.6569C15.1571 12.1566 16 10.1217 16 8C16 5.87827 15.1571 3.84344 13.6569 2.34315C12.1566 0.842855 10.1217 0 8 0C5.87827 0 3.84344 0.842855 2.34314 2.34315C0.842853 3.84344 0 5.87827 0 8C0 10.1217 0.842853 12.1566 2.34314 13.6569C3.84344 15.1571 5.87827 16 8 16ZM6.75 10.5H7.5V8.5H6.75H6V7H6.75H8.25H9V7.75V10.5H9.25H10V12H9.25H6.75H6V10.5H6.75ZM9 6H7V4H9V6Z" fill="black"></path></g></svg></button></span></div><span><div class="as-of-date oneds-body-s-compact" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-threeYrBetaFund-asOf" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-threeYrBetaFund-asOf">as of -</div></span></th><td class="data oneds-body-l-bold" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-threeYrBetaFund" tabindex="-1" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-threeYrBetaFund-data">-</td></tr><tr class="data-item oneds-body-m-compact col-priceBook" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-row-priceBook"><th class="caption" tabindex="-1"><div class="caption-wrapper"><span class="label" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-priceBook-label" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-priceBook-label">P/B Ratio</span><span class="info-bubble-container"><button id="infoBubble-7d57d42e-31ff-42c9-ab28-e1f74e39e689" class="product-info-bubble" aria-haspopup="true" aria-label="More Info: " aria-expanded="false" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-priceBook-infoBubble" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-priceBook-infoBubble" title="The price to book (P/B) value ratio is a fundamental measure used to determine if an investment is valued appropriately. The book value of a company is a measure of how much a company&#x27;s assets are worth assuming the company&#x27;s debts are paid off. Negative book values are excluded from this calculation and holding price to book ratios over 25 are set to 25."><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 18 16" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><g id="Circle-info"><path id="Vector" d="M8 16C10.1217 16 12.1566 15.1571 13.6569 13.6569C15.1571 12.1566 16 10.1217 16 8C16 5.87827 15.1571 3.84344 13.6569 2.34315C12.1566 0.842855 10.1217 0 8 0C5.87827 0 3.84344 0.842855 2.34314 2.34315C0.842853 3.84344 0 5.87827 0 8C0 10.1217 0.842853 12.1566 2.34314 13.6569C3.84344 15.1571 5.87827 16 8 16ZM6.75 10.5H7.5V8.5H6.75H6V7H6.75H8.25H9V7.75V10.5H9.25H10V12H9.25H6.75H6V10.5H6.75ZM9 6H7V4H9V6Z" fill="black"></path></g></svg></button></span></div><span><div class="as-of-date oneds-body-s-compact" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-priceBook-asOf" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-priceBook-asOf">as of 22/Sept/2026</div></span></th><td class="data oneds-body-l-bold" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-priceBook" tabindex="-1" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-priceBook-data">4.06</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div><div class="one-column reverse-striping"><div class="_tableWrapper_1a71w_3" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-table-right-column" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-table-right-column"><div class="_scrollShadow_1a71w_17 _left_1a71w_29"></div><div class="_scrollShadow_1a71w_17 _right_1a71w_33"></div><div class="_scrollContainer_1a71w_7 _freeHeight_1a71w_14"><table class="facts-table"><tbody class="facts-table-body"><tr class="data-item oneds-body-m-compact col-levelAmount" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-row-levelAmount"><th class="caption" tabindex="-1"><div class="caption-wrapper"><span class="label" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-levelAmount-label" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-levelAmount-label">Benchmark Level</span></div><span><div class="as-of-date oneds-body-s-compact" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-levelAmount-asOf" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-levelAmount-asOf">as of 23/Sept/2026</div></span></th><td class="data oneds-body-l-bold" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-levelAmount" tabindex="-1" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-levelAmount-data">USD <!-- -->5,220.53</td></tr><tr class="data-item oneds-body-m-compact col-volatilitySourced3YrAnnualized" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-row-volatilitySourced3YrAnnualized"><th class="caption" tabindex="-1"><div class="caption-wrapper"><span class="label" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-volatilitySourced3YrAnnualized-label" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-volatilitySourced3YrAnnualized-label">Standard Deviation (3y)</span><span class="info-bubble-container"><button id="infoBubble-94f1abac-fa21-420b-ad9e-fda1fd687924" class="product-info-bubble" aria-haspopup="true" aria-label="More Info: " aria-expanded="false" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-volatilitySourced3YrAnnualized-infoBubble" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-volatilitySourced3YrAnnualized-infoBubble" title="Standard deviation measures how dispersed returns are around the average. A higher standard deviation indicates that returns are spread out over a larger range of values and thus, more volatile."><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 18 16" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><g id="Circle-info"><path id="Vector" d="M8 16C10.1217 16 12.1566 15.1571 13.6569 13.6569C15.1571 12.1566 16 10.1217 16 8C16 5.87827 15.1571 3.84344 13.6569 2.34315C12.1566 0.842855 10.1217 0 8 0C5.87827 0 3.84344 0.842855 2.34314 2.34315C0.842853 3.84344 0 5.87827 0 8C0 10.1217 0.842853 12.1566 2.34314 13.6569C3.84344 15.1571 5.87827 16 8 16ZM6.75 10.5H7.5V8.5H6.75H6V7H6.75H8.25H9V7.75V10.5H9.25H10V12H9.25H6.75H6V10.5H6.75ZM9 6H7V4H9V6Z" fill="black"></path></g></svg></button></span></div><span><div class="as-of-date oneds-body-s-compact" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-volatilitySourced3YrAnnualized-asOf" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-volatilitySourced3YrAnnualized-asOf">as of -</div></span></th><td class="data oneds-body-l-bold" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-volatilitySourced3YrAnnualized" tabindex="-1" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-volatilitySourced3YrAnnualized-data">-</td></tr><tr class="data-item oneds-body-m-compact col-priceEarnings" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-row-priceEarnings"><th class="caption" tabindex="-1"><div class="caption-wrapper"><span class="label" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-priceEarnings-label" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-priceEarnings-label">P/E Ratio</span><span class="info-bubble-container"><button id="infoBubble-8e4bb202-1072-4502-9495-9b18e314b90a" class="product-info-bubble" aria-haspopup="true" aria-label="More Info: " aria-expanded="false" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-priceEarnings-infoBubble" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-priceEarnings-infoBubble" title="The price to earnings ratio (P/E) is a fundamental measure used to determine if an investment is valued appropriately. Each holdings&#x27; P/E is the latest closing price divided by the latest 12 months&#x27; earnings per share. Negative earnings are excluded, extraordinary items are excluded, and P/E ratios over 60 are set to 60."><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 18 16" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><g id="Circle-info"><path id="Vector" d="M8 16C10.1217 16 12.1566 15.1571 13.6569 13.6569C15.1571 12.1566 16 10.1217 16 8C16 5.87827 15.1571 3.84344 13.6569 2.34315C12.1566 0.842855 10.1217 0 8 0C5.87827 0 3.84344 0.842855 2.34314 2.34315C0.842853 3.84344 0 5.87827 0 8C0 10.1217 0.842853 12.1566 2.34314 13.6569C3.84344 15.1571 5.87827 16 8 16ZM6.75 10.5H7.5V8.5H6.75H6V7H6.75H8.25H9V7.75V10.5H9.25H10V12H9.25H6.75H6V10.5H6.75ZM9 6H7V4H9V6Z" fill="black"></path></g></svg></button></span></div><span><div class="as-of-date oneds-body-s-compact" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-priceEarnings-asOf" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-priceEarnings-asOf">as of 22/Sept/2026</div></span></th><td class="data oneds-body-l-bold" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-priceEarnings" tabindex="-1" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-priceEarnings-data">25.85</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></div><div class="info-bubble-tooltip-container oneds-body-m-compact"><div id="tooltip"><div id="tooltipText"></div></div></div></div></div></walrus-render-on-client></div><div data-componentname="feeTable"></div><div data-componentname="riskIndicator"></div><div data-componentname="ratingsAndAwards"><walrus-render-on-client componenttype="on-server-first" componentprops="{&quot;componentId&quot;:&quot;ratingsAndAwards&quot;,&quot;properties&quot;:{&quot;minLipperRating&quot;:&quot;3&quot;,&q